	"about": {
		"text": "Cheese whose curd is pressed and ripened for about one to three months, firm enough to cut cleanly into slices: under German cheese law it holds more than 54 and up to 63 % water in the cheese without its fat. Germany calls it Schnittkäse, cheese for slicing; Gouda, Edam and Tilsiter are among them.",
